abstract: >-
  scaleinvariance provides tools for simulating and analyzing scale-invariant
  and multifractal fields. Simulation covers fractionally integrated flux
  (multiplicative cascades) in 1-D and N-D, fractional Brownian motion by
  spectral synthesis and by fractional integration, and generalized scale
  invariance for anisotropic scaling. Analysis covers Hurst exponent
  estimation by structure functions, Haar and general wavelet fluctuations,
  and spectra, together with intermittency estimators for the moment scaling
  function K(q). All routines run on numpy or, optionally, torch (CPU or GPU),
  support N-dimensional arrays, and handle both periodic and non-periodic
  domains.
